---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");

const PAGES = [
  ["/decisions", "Decisions",
   "Every choice that could have gone the other way, and what it cost."],
  ["/process", "Process",
   "What actually happened over three days, including five bugs we shipped and caught."],
  ["/limits", "Limits",
   "What DiresQ does not do. Written down rather than hoped over."],
  ["/api", "API",
   "Every endpoint, what it takes, and what comes back."],
];
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>DiresQ — tracking the people going in</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Every disaster app tells you where the disaster is. DiresQ tracks the people going into it."
    />
    <link rel="icon" href={`${base}/favicon.ico`} />
  </head>

  <body>
    <main class="hero">
      <p class="kicker">Katy Youth Hacks 2026 · Tech for Humanity</p>
      <h1>DiresQ</h1>

      <p class="thesis">
        Every disaster app tells you where the disaster is.
        <strong>DiresQ tracks the people going into it.</strong>
      </p>

      <p class="body">
        When a flood hits, volunteers self-deploy — a neighbour with a boat, a
        cousin with a truck. Nobody logs it. Four people end up at the same
        car in a creek while a street two blocks away has nobody at all, and
        when someone stops answering their phone, there is no record that they
        ever went out.
      </p>

      <p class="body">
        DiresQ logs who went where, holds them to a check-in timer, and turns
        the board red when somebody goes quiet. If they stay quiet, it files a
        report about them at their last known position, because a red row only
        helps if somebody is looking at the board.
      </p>

      <nav class="cards">
        {PAGES.map(([href, title, blurb]) => (
          <a href={`${base}${href}`}>
            <h2>{title}</h2>
            <p>{blurb}</p>
          </a>
        ))}
      </nav>

      <p class="repo">
        <a href="https://github.com/Londopy/DiresQ">Source on GitHub</a>
      </p>
    </main>

    <style is:global>
      :root {
        --base: #1e1e2e;
        --mantle: #181825;
        --surface: #313244;
        --text: #cdd6f4;
        --subtext: #a6adc8;
        --blue: #89b4fa;
        --green: #a6e3a1;
        --red: #f38ba8;
      }

      * { box-sizing: border-box; }

      body {
        margin: 0;
        background: var(--base);
        color: var(--text);
        font: 16px/1.65 system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
      }

      .hero { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 90px 24px 80px; }

      .kicker {
        margin: 0 0 10px;
        color: var(--subtext);
        font-size: 13px;
        letter-spacing: 1.5px;
        text-transform: uppercase;
      }

      h1 {
        margin: 0 0 22px;
        font-size: 64px;
        letter-spacing: -1px;
        color: var(--green);
      }

      .thesis { margin: 0 0 28px; font-size: 22px; line-height: 1.45; }
      .thesis strong { color: var(--red); }

      .body { margin: 0 0 18px; color: var(--subtext); }

      .cards {
        display: grid;
        gap: 14px;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(230px, 1fr));
        margin: 44px 0 32px;
      }

      .cards a {
        display: block;
        padding: 18px;
        border-radius: 10px;
        background: var(--surface);
        text-decoration: none;
        color: inherit;
        border-left: 3px solid transparent;
      }

      .cards a:hover { border-left-color: var(--blue); }

      .cards h2 { margin: 0 0 6px; font-size: 17px; color: var(--blue); }
      .cards p { margin: 0; font-size: 14px; color: var(--subtext); }

      .repo { font-size: 14px; }
      a { color: var(--blue); }

      @media (max-width: 560px) {
        .hero { padding: 56px 20px 60px; }
        h1 { font-size: 44px; }
        .thesis { font-size: 19px; }
      }
    </style>
  </body>
</html>
